'==============================================================
' Description:
'   Sequence diagram showing the end-to-end flow when a user
'   adds a new Workout in the Workout Tracker application.
'   The diagram abstracts away specific method names to focus
'   on logical interactions between layers:
'       - UI (View & Controller)
'       - Client-side service and REST client
'       - Server-side REST API and file persistence.
'
' Notes:
'   • Method names are omitted intentionally to emphasize 
'     system responsibilities and message flow rather than 
'     specific code implementation.
'   • Includes color-coded notes:
'         > lightsteelblue: UI
'         > lightskyblue: core
'         > aqua: server
'         > palegreen: persistence
'
' Extensions to download for preview to work:
'   • PlantUML extension (jebbs)
'   • PlantUML Previewer (Mebrahtom Guesh)
'   (Click Ctrl + P to preview)
'==============================================================

@startuml sequence-diagram
'--- Styling ---
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 15
skinparam sequenceParticipant underline
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
autonumber "<b>[0]"

title <b>Sequence: User adds a new Workout</b>\n(UI → REST → JSON file)

actor User #LightSkyBlue

box "Client Application" #LightYellow
    participant "WorkoutFormView" as View
    control "WorkoutFormController" as Form
    control "WorkoutService (client)" as Service
    collections "WorkoutTracker" as Tracker
    boundary "WorkoutRestClient" as RestClient
end box

box "Server (Spring Boot)" #LightBlue
    control "WorkoutController (REST)" as ServerCtrl
    control "WorkoutService (server)" as ServerSvc
    database "WorkoutFileManager" as FileManager
end box

'--- Flow ---
User -> View: Fill in input fields
User -> View: Click <b>"Add Workout"</b>
activate View
View -> Form: Submit workout input
activate Form


group Validation and Creation
    note right of Form #lightsteelblue
        Exercises are stored locally until
        the user submits the Workout 
    end note
    
    note right of Form #lightsteelblue
        Validates input fields before creating
        the Workout object
    end note

    Form -> Form: create Workout from Exercises and input
end

Form -> Service: Send new Workout to service
activate Service

Service -> RestClient: Send Workout to server
activate RestClient
note right of Service #lightskyblue
    WorkoutService delegates REST call
    to WorkoutRestClient
end note

note right of RestClient #lightskyblue: Serialize object\nand send HTTP request
RestClient -> ServerCtrl: HTTP POST /api/workouts
activate ServerCtrl

group Server Processing
    ServerCtrl -> ServerSvc: Request to persist Workout
    note right of ServerCtrl #aqua
        REST Controller delegates storage
        responsibility to Service layer
    end note
    activate ServerSvc
    note right of ServerSvc #aqua: Adds Workout to list
    ServerSvc -> FileManager: Save Workout to file
    activate FileManager
    note right of FileManager #palegreen: Write to data/workouts.json
    FileManager --> ServerSvc: success
    deactivate FileManager
    ServerSvc --> ServerCtrl: return saved Workout (with ID)
    deactivate ServerSvc
end

ServerCtrl --> RestClient: HTTP 201 Created
deactivate ServerCtrl
RestClient --> Service: Return created Workout
deactivate RestClient

Service -> Tracker: Update local workout list
activate Tracker
note right of Tracker #lightskyblue
    Adds created Workout to ObservableList
    so UI table updates automatically
end note
Tracker --> User: Show updated workout list in TableView 
deactivate Tracker

Service --> Form: success
deactivate Service

note left of Form #lightsteelblue
    MainController does the navigation
    from WorkoutFormview to WorkoutTableView.
end note
Form -> View: Navigate to WorkoutTableView
View --> User: Show updated list
deactivate Form
deactivate View

@enduml
